From b465fa0591b2664808c3293f153a2c0944fd125f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:40:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix hit registration without line of sight

A hit on an entity whose eyes are not in line of sight of the attacker's
eyes was only accepted within 3 blocks (feet to feet) instead of 6. A
slab, fence or ledge between the two heads therefore dropped ordinary
3-block hits, because feet-to-feet distance of a legit hit often exceeds
3 blocks. Keep the 6 block check in all cases (PandaSpigot GH-244).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PlayerConnection.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PlayerConnection.java
index d47e4667..a54bed5b 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PlayerConnection.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PlayerConnection.java
@@ -1337,7 +1337,7 @@ public class PlayerConnection implements PacketListenerPlayIn, IUpdatePlayerList
             boolean flag = this.player.hasLineOfSight(entity);
             double d0 = 36.0D;
 
-            if (!flag) {
+            if (false && !flag) { // CubingPaper - Fix hit registration (PandaSpigot GH-244): no 3-block reach limit without line of sight
                 d0 = 9.0D;
             }
 
